The product doesn't ship model weights. `lmt models download` downloads these models from
Hugging Face, each at a pinned revision, under its own licence:

- Systran/faster-distil-whisper-large-v3 (speech recognition): MIT License.
  Model card: https://huggingface.co/Systran/faster-distil-whisper-large-v3

- pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1 (the diarization pipeline): MIT License.
  Model card: https://huggingface.co/pyannote/speaker-diarization-3.1

- pyannote/segmentation-3.0 (speaker segmentation): MIT License.
  Model card: https://huggingface.co/pyannote/segmentation-3.0

- pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM (speaker embeddings): Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.
  Attribution: "wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM", published by pyannote on Hugging Face,
  https://huggingface.co/pyannote/wespeaker-voxceleb-resnet34-LM. Used unmodified.

The product doesn't ship its dependencies either: they install from PyPI (and, for torch and
torchaudio on Linux, the PyTorch CPU index), each under its own licence. toolchain.toml's
[licences] section lists every licence and bundled library that CI checks. Some of them ask
for these notices:

- Portions of this software are copyright (C) The FreeType Project (https://freetype.org).
  All rights reserved. (FreeType, inside pillow's wheel, under the FreeType License.)

- This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group. (libjpeg-turbo,
  inside pillow's wheel.)

- pillow is under the MIT-CMU License, regex under Apache-2.0 and the CNRI Python licence,
  and numpy partly under the zlib licence. Each wheel carries its notice in its .dist-info.

- PyAV's (av) wheels bundle FFmpeg (LGPL-3.0-or-later), the x264 and x265 video encoders
  (GPL-2.0-or-later) and LAME (LGPL-2.0-or-later). soundfile's wheels bundle libsndfile with
  LAME and mpg123 (LGPL). Each is a shared library under its own licence, unmodified. The
  product only decodes audio and never calls the x264 or x265 encoders.
